{"before_validation modifies self.host in place but will throw if host is nil - needs host.present? check before sub! calls": 0.9181652069091797, "Admin::EmbeddableHostsController#update and #destroy don't guard against missing records - if id not found, host will be nil and calling methods will raise NoMethodError": 0.8185797333717346, "Migration SQL insertion is vulnerable to SQL injection - raw SQL interpolates host strings directly without escaping, which can break or allow injection if host contains single quotes or malicious input": 0.950711190700531, "Migration assumes site_settings rows exist and returns value arrays, which is brittle and may fail on different DB adapters": 0.551788866519928, "EmbeddableHost model has belongs_to :category but no validates_presence_of :category_id despite DB having NOT NULL constraint": 0.20399293303489685, "save_host(host) assumes params[:embeddable_host] exists without strong params guard": 0.33439478278160095, "Controllers use deprecated before_filter instead of before_action (for newer Rails versions)": 0.012833066284656525, "EmbeddableHost host validation regex is too strict - rejects valid hostnames with TLDs longer than 5 chars, IDNs, IPv6 addresses": 0.29525700211524963, "TopicEmbed.import: if EmbeddableHost.record_for_host returns nil, category_id will be nil but should potentially fall back to SiteSetting.uncategorized_category_id": 0.21153855323791504, "EmbeddableHost.record_for_host returns false if URL invalid instead of nil, which is inconsistent": 0.1289854198694229, "Admin::EmbeddingController#update doesn't actually persist any changes - just renders @embedding": 0.3716990649700165, "Admin::EmbeddableHostsController#create/update missing strong params (permit host, category_id) to avoid mass-assignment issues": 0.339588463306427, "Fabricator files appear to have exchanged contents - category_fabricator.rb was replaced by embeddable_host fabricator content, which could confuse maintainers and cause loading order issues": 0.8793008327484131}